[Bug]: connectOverCDP replaces the page's main frame with a nested sandboxed iframe when its parentFrameId is unknown

### Version

1.63.0

### Steps to reproduce

Self-contained, Playwright-only (Node's `http` server plus the bundled Chromium, spawned with `--remote-debugging-port` so the page is fully loaded **before** `connectOverCDP`):

1. `npm i playwright@1.63.0 && npx playwright install chromium`
2. Save the script below as `repro.mjs` and run `node repro.mjs`

The page shape that triggers it: top document (127.0.0.1) > cross-site iframe (localhost, out of process) > same-process child iframe > `sandbox` `srcdoc` iframe (its own `iframe` target).

```js
// connectOverCDP to an already-loaded page: the Page's main frame is replaced by a
// nested out-of-process iframe. Page shape: top (127.0.0.1) > cross-site iframe
// (localhost) > same-process child iframe > sandboxed srcdoc iframe.
import http from 'node:http';
import { spawn } from 'node:child_process';
import { mkdtempSync } from 'node:fs';
import { tmpdir } from 'node:os';
import { join } from 'node:path';
import { chromium } from 'playwright';

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  const port = server.address().port;
  const pages = {
    '/': `<h1 id=top>TOP</h1><iframe src="http://localhost:${port}/b"></iframe>`,
    '/b': `<iframe src="/c"></iframe>`,
    '/c': `<iframe sandbox="allow-scripts" srcdoc="<p>D</p>"></iframe>`,
  };
  res.setHeader('content-type', 'text/html');
  res.end(pages[req.url] ?? '');
}).listen(0, '127.0.0.1');
await new Promise(r => server.once('listening', r));
const url = `http://127.0.0.1:${server.address().port}/`;

// Chrome with the page already loaded before Playwright connects.
const chrome = spawn(process.env.CHROME || chromium.executablePath(), [
  '--headless=new', '--remote-debugging-port=9333', '--no-first-run',
  `--user-data-dir=${mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), 'pw-repro-'))}`, url,
], { stdio: 'ignore' });
for (let i = 0; i < 100; i++) {
  try { const r = await fetch('http://127.0.0.1:9333/json/list'); if ((await r.json()).some(t => t.url === url)) break; } catch {}
  await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 200));
}
await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 2000)); // let all frames load

const browser = await chromium.connectOverCDP('http://127.0.0.1:9333');
try {
const pages = browser.contexts().flatMap(c => c.pages());
console.log('expected top url     :', url);
console.log('pages()              :', pages.map(p => p.url()));
const page = pages.find(p => p.url() === url) ?? pages.find(p => !p.url().startsWith('chrome'));
console.log('page.url()           :', page.url());
console.log('evaluate location    :', await page.evaluate(() => location.href));
console.log('window.top === window:', await page.evaluate(() => window.top === window));
console.log('frames()             :', page.frames().map(f => f.url()));
console.log('locator("#top")      :', await page.locator('#top').count());

} catch (e) {
  console.log('ERROR                :', e.message.split('\n')[0]);
} finally {
  await browser.close();
  chrome.kill();
  server.close();
}
```

### Expected behavior

The page returned by `connectOverCDP` evaluates in its top-level document: `location.href` is the top URL, `window.top === window` is `true`, and `locator('#top')` finds the element.

### Actual behavior

The Page's main frame is replaced by the nested iframe.

- Playwright 1.63.0 + bundled Chromium 153.0.8010.12 (v1243): `page.evaluate` throws `Execution context was destroyed, most likely because of a navigation` in 8 of 8 runs (2 of 3 in an earlier batch), even though nothing navigates.
- Playwright 1.63.0 (and 1.60.0) through the Python binding, same page shape, Chrome for Testing 149.0.7827.55 (v1228): `page.evaluate("location.href")` returns `about:srcdoc`, `page.frames` lists only the top URL, and `locator("#top").count()` is 0. Every call runs inside the sandboxed srcdoc frame, and keyboard input doesn't reach the top document.

It first showed up on a real site whose ad stack nests sandboxed srcdoc frames inside cross-site ad iframes. Once the ads had loaded, every fresh `connectOverCDP` returned a page whose `evaluate` ran inside an ad frame (`location.href === 'about:srcdoc'`, `window.top !== window`), while raw `Runtime.evaluate` on a page-level CDP session still reached the real document.

### Additional context

The likely cause is in the `iframe` branch of `FrameSession._onAttachedToTarget` ([crPage.ts](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/b9a34ac7783a1b6c2e1dfff0c08ac744c048fa59/packages/playwright-core/src/server/chromium/crPage.ts#L759-L763)):

```ts
if (!frame && event.targetInfo.parentFrameId) {
  frame = this._page.frameManager.frameAttached(targetId, event.targetInfo.parentFrameId);
}
```

When `parentFrameId` names a frame the FrameManager has never registered (here, the same-process child of an out-of-process iframe on an already-loaded page), `FrameManager.frameAttached` ([frames.ts](https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/b9a34ac7783a1b6c2e1dfff0c08ac744c048fa59/packages/playwright-core/src/server/frames.ts#L168-L174)) finds no parent and takes the "no parent" path. That path renames the **main frame** to the iframe's id (`this._mainFrame._id = frameId`), and the child session's execution contexts then bind to the main frame.

The same file already guards the frame-tree path against an unknown parent (`if (parentFrameId && !this._page.frameManager.frame(parentFrameId)) return;` in `_onFrameAttached`). Applying the same check here made the repro pass 8 of 8 runs locally (patched `coreBundle.js`, 1.63.0, Chromium v1243):

```ts
if (!frame && event.targetInfo.parentFrameId && this._page.frameManager.frame(event.targetInfo.parentFrameId)) {
```

With that guard the nested frames are skipped rather than attached (the same limitation as #17656), but the Page keeps its real main frame.

Related: #17656 (the `parentFrameId` attach path came from its fix), #36095. Neither covers the main-frame replacement.

### Environment

```
OS: macOS 15.7.7 (x86_64)
Node: 26.3.0
playwright: 1.63.0 (also reproduced with 1.60.0 via playwright-python)
Browsers: Chromium 153.0.8010.12 (playwright v1243); Chrome for Testing 149.0.7827.55 (v1228)
```

